# Normalise line endings so the committed blob is always LF, whatever the checkout does.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF in the working tree while the blob stays LF. Without this file that arrangement is
# invisible to git but not to Prettier: `.prettierrc` sets `endOfLine: lf`, so
# `npm run format:check` read every CRLF working-tree file as a style failure and reported
# 371 files — of which the overwhelming majority were the checkout, not the content.
#
# A checker whose output is mostly noise is a checker nobody runs, and nobody did: that is
# why `format:check` sits outside `npm run ci` (see .agents/rules/ecc/PROJECT-OVERRIDES.md).
# `tools/verify-memory-archive.mjs` documents the same trap from the other side — it once
# reported 387 CRLF failures on a perfectly clean tree.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git to store text as LF and check it out as LF on every platform,
# so the working tree, the blob and Prettier finally agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
